{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <queue>\n#include <climits>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing llong = long long;\nusing P = pair<llong, int>;\n\nconst int MAXN = 5500;\nconst llong INF = 1000000007LL;\n\nint n, m, k, c, d;\nint src, dst;\nint flow = 0;\nllong cost = 0;\nllong ddist[MAXN];\nint par[MAXN];\n\nstruct Edge {\n    int to;\n    int w;\n    int rev;\n    int cap;\n};\n\nvector<Edge> g[MAXN];\n\nvoid link(int u, int v, int w, int cap) {\n    int sz1 = g[u].size(), sz2 = g[v].size();\n    g[u].push_back({v, w, sz2, cap});\n    g[v].push_back({u, -w, sz1, 0});\n}\n\nvoid spfa() {\n    fill(ddist, ddist + MAXN, INF);\n    queue<int> q;\n    ddist[src] = 0;\n    q.push(src);\n    \n    while (!q.empty()) {\n        int u = q.front(); q.pop();\n        for (const auto& e : g[u]) {\n            if (e.cap > 0 && ddist[e.to] > ddist[u] + e.w) {\n                ddist[e.to] = ddist[u] + e.w;\n                par[e.to] = e.rev;\n                q.push(e.to);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvoid path_augment() {\n    int f = k;\n    int cur = dst;\n    while (cur != src) {\n        int prev = g[cur][par[cur]].to;\n        int idx = g[cur][par[cur]].rev;\n        f = min(f, g[prev][idx].cap);\n        cur = prev;\n    }\n    \n    flow += f;\n    cost += f * ddist[dst];\n    \n    cur = dst;\n    while (cur != src) {\n        int prev = g[cur][par[cur]].to;\n        int idx = g[cur][par[cur]].rev;\n        g[cur][par[cur]].cap += f;\n        g[prev][idx].cap -= f;\n        cur = prev;\n    }\n}\n\nint idx(int v, int t) {\n    return v + t * n;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> n >> m >> k >> c >> d;\n    src = MAXN - 2;\n    dst = MAXN - 1;\n    int T = n + k;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        cin >> u;\n        link(src, idx(u, 0), 0, 1);\n    }\n    \n    for (int t = 0; t <= T; ++t) {\n        link(idx(1, t), dst, c * t, k);\n    }\n    \n    for (int v = 1; v <= n; ++v) {\n        for (int t = 0; t < T; ++t) {\n            link(idx(v, t), idx(v, t + 1), 0, k);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    while (m--) {\n        cin >> u >> v;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; ++i) {\n            for (int t = 0; t < T; ++t) {\n                int w = d * (2 * i - 1);\n                link(idx(u, t), idx(v, t + 1), w, 1);\n                link(idx(v, t), idx(u, t + 1), w, 1);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    while (flow < k) {\n        spfa();\n        path_augment();\n    }\n    \n    cout << cost;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    it = iter(data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    m = int(next(it))\n    k = int(next(it))\n    c = int(next(it))\n    d = int(next(it))\n    \n    MAXN = 5500\n    INF = 1000000007\n    \n    src = MAXN - 2\n    dst = MAXN - 1\n    T = n + k\n    \n   